{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763775-this-story-is-true-rumors-of-the-forsaken-add-your-own","id":763775,"title":"This Story is True. [Rumors of the Forsaken, add your own]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T22:22:28-08:00","id":763775,"title":"This Story is True. [Rumors of the Forsaken, add your own]","content":"<i>The thing about entering a Hunter's Territory? is that it's unlikely you'll be able to leave it without their express permission. You know how they deal with Anshega trespassing? They drive them to a frothing rage, they all Kuruth. Usually it only takes killing their weakest in the swiftest way possible. Other times they have specific spirits pressed into that task, who would feast at the unleashed fury. But then they can't leave that patch of land. One by one, they collapse. If they don't eat each other, the Hunters come back and simply slit the throats of the bastards while they're unconscious. That's why you always make sure you're welcome in their mus-rah. They won't find your body otherwise.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T22:40:38-08:00","id":763786,"title":"","content":"<i>Heard something curious from the chatter of the Radio choir while on sabbatical in Cape Canaveral. Supposedly Luna's dark side changes form on a less predictable timetable than the face we see. How much strength must the Warden Moon's task require of her out in the void if our race was spawned by her idlest aspect?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T07:53:38-08:00","id":764050,"title":"","content":"<i>There was this thing, this horrible thing shuddering and humming and cutting through them like they were nothing. I thought it was a rescue, at first, then maybe a Predator King killing rivals or a hound of the Bale. But when they were all dead it stood in front of me, furless, with rubbery grey skin, changing out of gauru.<br /> <br /> And it turned into a spirit. This wasn't some Claimed, or a trick like the Ithaeur. I could see its brands, they hurt my eyes to look at and made no sense but it wasn't of the Crescent Moon. It turned into a spirit and it howled, it howled this howl that sounded like that noise, the feedback when you get the mic too close to the speaker and my ears started bleeding. It ripped the silver runes of my renown right out of me.<br /> <br /> It. I keep saying it but it was a woman, very clearly a female Uratha, even in spirit form. She said, in the First Tongue, my ears were still healing so it wasn't clear but she said she was Arkozy of the Tind'losi Tribe, and she said something about a Vampire Moon. Then she zipped away and it was like she was never there, I couldn't find a trace of her.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-12-2015, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T10:23:23-08:00","id":764177,"title":"","content":"<i>You know about that one family that's always had atleast one werewolf every generation since the Colonial days? I hear that the family's fallen under some hard times and been unable to have atleast someone new in the family grow a nice pelt for the past thirty years. Won't be long now before their uninterrupted line of succession ends, but something tells me they aren't going to take that just lying down. They're up to something and I'm sure it breaks several rules.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:36:13-08:00","id":764556,"title":"","content":"<i>Supposedly there is an Ivory Claw lodge that serves an ancestor spirit that was the ideal of crooked salesman, the lodge of Honest George. Supposedly, they''ll sell their products, most famously Steel Wolf fetishes and computers that are just too good to be true, to anyone, forsaken, pure, bale, vampire, wizard, even normal humans !. Of course, most of the product is defective in some amusing way (especially what they sell to the Bale Hounds) but once in awhile they sell something that actually works as amazingly as promised. From what I understand, the lodge is run as a corporation by one Claw family who got their start as traveling shady merchants in the middle ages, then added crooked car salesmen to their resume in the 30s, branched out into computers when the similarities between computer and car salesmen dawned on on of the family's younger members in the 90s and are now involved in all sorts of scams via their megacorp.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the reason I'm telling you all this is because my contacts among the local fairies (who seem to have some history with these guys) say a member of the family that runs the lodge is moving a big shipment through town to sell at some hidden market the fay told me about. Normally I wouldn't give a shit about shoddy merch from a crooked claw family, except that this particular member of the family specializes in selling art and antiquities, and rumor has that among all the forged artwork is something that dates back to the Forsaken of ancient Sumer and we can't let an Ivory Claw sell our heritage to the highest bidder now, can we?</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T07:16:29-08:00","id":767046,"title":"","content":"<i>I'm not one to speak ill of Family, but that new member of my brood, Ivan? He's a black sheep among black sheep. Says he is a 'Predator King', which I think is like being an Adventist, or maybe a Democrat - whatever - but the thing is, I think he's smart. Smarter than any of his brothers and sisters, and he's -my- little cousin.<br /> <br /> Check this out. He says there are little 'spirits' that make up bigger ones. Rats have a rat-king, Spiders have a spider-queen, same I guess with eagles and weasles and aardvarks? He says he's the same. Wolves. Something bad happened in a long-ago and I guess some titanic old Beast that abandoned Flesh for the Dream literally fell to pieces at the sight of the moon.<br /> <br /> He's going to find them. Gather them all up, eat them whole. He says their beating hearts will make him stronger. He wants to do this Highlander shit - says if there's only one, that maybe it will be his Old Papa Wolf. They will all be together again. Strong again.<br /> <br /> I'll admit I'm curious. Maybe I'll help him. He says they're all Hunters... But that's just code for bullies, picking on weaker Prey. And you know how I feel about bullies. Punishing them? Making -them- the victim? If he goes all the way, maybe I can have a nice long 'talk' with his father about how he's been such a bad boy. Maybe I won't be so Hungry anymore.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T12:51:17-08:00","id":768679,"title":"","content":"<i>What I'm about to say is true...or, whatever it is we're supposed to say before these things.<br /> <br /> There's a big, nasty Wound over in Lubbock. It's causing all sorts of trouble. But the local packs apparently have it well in hand, despite numbering less than a baker's dozen.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Some of my friends thought this was suspicious. They took a trip over there, just to see what was going on. The local packs didn't want them to come in. You figure that's just the </i>Meninna<i> being themselves, but these guys are apparently all </i>Iminir, <i>so that idea's right out. So my buddies hop over to the </i>hisil<i> to try and sneak by. Only one came back, said that she was ambushed by the locals and she was the only one to successfully get away.<br /> <br /> She said the whole city is almost covered in webs. Big, thick, Spirit-choking webs.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}